1. Windows ExifTool experiment – command cheat sheet
Step 1: Check the extracted ExifTool folder
dir D:\


Step 2: Check the contents of your extracted folder
dir "D:\exiftool-13.55_64"


Step 3: Rename the executable
ren "D:\exiftool-13.55_64\exiftool(-k).exe" exiftool.exe


Step 4: Check the ExifTool version
"D:\exiftool-13.55_64\exiftool.exe" -ver


Step 5: Create the experiment folders
mkdir D:\DMF
mkdir D:\DMF\Experiment1


Step 6: Move image1.HEIC into the experiment folder using File Explorer.

Step 7: Open the experiment folder in CMD
cd /d D:\DMF\Experiment1


Step 8: Verify the image is present
dir


Step 9: Extract all image metadata
"D:\exiftool-13.55_64\exiftool.exe" image1.HEIC


Step 10: Extract detailed metadata
"D:\exiftool-13.55_64\exiftool.exe" -G1 -a -s image1.HEIC


Step 11: Save metadata into a text file
"D:\exiftool-13.55_64\exiftool.exe" -G1 -a -s image1.HEIC > metadata_output.txt


Step 12: Extract GPS information
"D:\exiftool-13.55_64\exiftool.exe" -GPSLatitude -GPSLongitude -GPSAltitude image1.HEIC


Step 13: Generate SHA-256 hash
certutil -hashfile image1.HEIC SHA256


Step 14: Verify the output files
dir


Note: If your extracted ExifTool folder has a different name, replace exiftool-13.55_64 in the commands with its actual folder name.

